Chapter: GopFiles
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopUsbKbd
  cites Works chapter GopUsbMouse
  cites Kernel chapter BitmapFont
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter CCE
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The file manager -- H4e's first app on the desktop. It browses the
 boot medium's ESP through the same GopFat16 mount every storage
 screen uses, riding the medium lock, so the volume on the glass is
 the volume the machine booted from. The list is the directory's
 decoded entries; Enter or a click descends into a directory or opens
 a byte view of a file; Esc climbs back up and finally returns to the
 desktop.

 The loop keeps the desk's law: idle is the keyboard mailbox take and
 the allocation-free mouse pump; everything that allocates -- a
 directory listing, a repaint, a sector read for the preview -- runs
 only when an event asks for it. The preview reads exactly one
 sector: the first 128 bytes name a file better than a two-megabyte
 read that would sit on a heap with no collector.

 We say:

Section: Palette and Geometry

  gfl-col-bg : Integer = #1B2440
  gfl-col-title : Integer = #2E5C8A
  gfl-col-text : Integer = #909CB0
  gfl-col-bright : Integer = #FFFFFF
  gfl-col-sel : Integer = #3A5C9A
  gfl-col-dim : Integer = #5A6478
  gfl-col-green : Integer = #00FF00

 The pane floats over the desktop to the right of the sidebar. Every
 measure derives from the panel rectangle and the scale, so the same
 code lays out 640x480 and 1280x800.

  gfl-px : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-px (w) (s) = 90 * s

  gfl-py : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-py (h) (s) = 30 * s

  gfl-pw : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-pw (w) (s) = w - 120 * s

  gfl-ph : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-ph (h) (s) = h - 74 * s

  gfl-row-h : Integer -> Integer
  gfl-row-h (s) = 18 * s

  gfl-rows-y0 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-rows-y0 (h) (s) = gfl-py h s + 44 * s

  gfl-rows-vis : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-rows-vis (h) (s) = (gfl-ph h s - 74 * s) / gfl-row-h s

 The row under a screen point, or -1: shared by hover and click so
 the two can never disagree about what the pointer is on.

  gfl-row-at : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-row-at (w) (h) (s) (top) (n) (mx) (my) =
    let y0 = gfl-rows-y0 h s
    in if mx < gfl-px w s then -1
    else if mx >= gfl-px w s + gfl-pw w s then -1
    else if my < y0 then -1
    else let row = top + (my - y0) / gfl-row-h s
    in if row >= n then -1
    else if row - top >= gfl-rows-vis h s then -1
    else row

  gfl-close-hit : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  gfl-close-hit (w) (h) (s) (mx) (my) =
    let bx = gfl-px w s + gfl-pw w s - 16 * s
    in if mx < bx then False
    else if mx >= gfl-px w s + gfl-pw w s then False
    else if my < gfl-py h s then False
    else if my >= gfl-py h s + 20 * s then False
    else True

 Keep the selection on screen: the top row follows the selection when
 it walks off either edge of the window.

  gfl-clamp-top : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-clamp-top (sel) (top) (vis) =
    if sel < top then sel
    else if sel >= top + vis then sel - vis + 1
    else top

Section: Formatting

  gfl-pad : Text, Integer -> Text
  gfl-pad (t) (width) =
    if text-length t >= width then t
    else gfl-pad (t & " ") width

  gfl-is-dir : Fat16DirEntry -> Boolean
  gfl-is-dir (e) = bit-and (e.de-attr) 16 == 16

  gfl-size-text : Fat16DirEntry -> Text
  gfl-size-text (e) = if gfl-is-dir e then "<DIR>" else show (e.de-size)

  gfl-row-text : Fat16DirEntry -> Text
  gfl-row-text (e) = gfl-pad (e.de-name) 16 & gfl-size-text e

  gfl-hex-digit : Integer -> Text
  gfl-hex-digit (v) =
    if v == 0 then "0" else if v == 1 then "1" else if v == 2 then "2"
    else if v == 3 then "3" else if v == 4 then "4" else if v == 5 then "5"
    else if v == 6 then "6" else if v == 7 then "7" else if v == 8 then "8"
    else if v == 9 then "9" else if v == 10 then "a" else if v == 11 then "b"
    else if v == 12 then "c" else if v == 13 then "d" else if v == 14 then "e"
    else "f"

  gfl-hex-byte : Integer -> Text
  gfl-hex-byte (b) = gfl-hex-digit (bit-and (bit-shru b 4) 15) & gfl-hex-digit (bit-and b 15)

  gfl-ascii : Integer -> Text
  gfl-ascii (c) =
    if c < 32 then "."
    else if c > 126 then "."
    else char-to-text (code-to-char (from-unicode c))

 One preview line: sixteen bytes as hex then the same sixteen as
 printable ASCII, the shape every hex viewer trains an eye for.

  gfl-hex-line : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  gfl-hex-line (buf) (off) (n) =
    gfl-hex-run buf off n "" & " " & gfl-ascii-run buf off n ""

  gfl-hex-run : Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  gfl-hex-run (buf) (off) (n) (acc) =
    if n == 0 then acc
    else gfl-hex-run buf (off + 1) (n - 1) (acc & gfl-hex-byte (peek-byte buf off) & " ")

  gfl-ascii-run : Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  gfl-ascii-run (buf) (off) (n) (acc) =
    if n == 0 then acc
    else gfl-ascii-run buf (off + 1) (n - 1) (acc & gfl-ascii (peek-byte buf off))

  gfl-path-text : List Text -> Text
  gfl-path-text (names) = gfl-path-loop names 0 "ESP:/"

  gfl-path-loop : List Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  gfl-path-loop (names) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length names then acc
    else gfl-path-loop names (i + 1) (acc & list-at names i & "/")

Section: Drawing

  gfl-draw-frame : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Text -> Integer
  gfl-draw-frame (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (title) =
    let px = gfl-px w s
    in let py = gfl-py h s
    in let pw = gfl-pw w s
    in let ph = gfl-ph h s
    in let body = gop-fill-rect base stride px py pw ph gfl-col-bg
    in let bar = gop-fill-rect base stride px py pw (20 * s) gfl-col-title
    in let cap = gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 6 * s) (py + 2 * s) title gfl-col-bright s 0
    in gop-draw-text base stride font (px + pw - 14 * s) (py + 2 * s) "x" gfl-col-bright s 0

  gfl-draw-rows : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, List Fat16DirEntry, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-draw-rows (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (entries) (sel) (top) (i) =
    let n = list-length entries
    in if top + i >= n then 0
    else if i >= gfl-rows-vis h s then 0
    else let idx = top + i
    in let y = gfl-rows-y0 h s + i * gfl-row-h s
    in let px = gfl-px w s
    in let hl = if idx == sel then gop-fill-rect base stride px y (gfl-pw w s) (gfl-row-h s) gfl-col-sel else 0
    in let e = list-at entries idx
    in let fg = if idx == sel then gfl-col-bright else if gfl-is-dir e then gfl-col-text else gfl-col-dim
    in let t = gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 10 * s) (y + s) (gfl-row-text e) fg s 0
    in gfl-draw-rows base w h stride s font entries sel top (i + 1)

  gfl-draw-list : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, List Fat16DirEntry, Integer, Integer, List Text -> Integer
  gfl-draw-list (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (entries) (sel) (top) (names) =
    let f = gfl-draw-frame base w h stride s font ("Files  " & gfl-path-text names)
    in let px = gfl-px w s
    in let py = gfl-py h s
    in let hdr = gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 10 * s) (py + 26 * s) (gfl-pad "name" 16 & "size") gfl-col-dim s 0
    in let rows = gfl-draw-rows base w h stride s font entries sel top 0
    in let none = if list-length entries == 0 then gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 10 * s) (gfl-rows-y0 h s) "(empty directory)" gfl-col-dim s 0 else 0
    in gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 10 * s) (py + gfl-ph h s - 18 * s) "Up/Down move   Enter open   Esc back" gfl-col-green s 0

  gfl-draw-preview : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Fat16DirEntry, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-draw-preview (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (e) (buf) (got) =
    let f = gfl-draw-frame base w h stride s font ("File  " & e.de-name)
    in let px = gfl-px w s
    in let py = gfl-py h s
    in let sz = gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 10 * s) (py + 26 * s) (show (e.de-size) & " bytes") gfl-col-bright s 0
    in let n = if got > 128 then 128 else got
    in let lines = gfl-preview-lines base w h stride s font buf 0 n
    in gop-draw-text base stride font (px + 10 * s) (py + gfl-ph h s - 18 * s) "Esc back" gfl-col-green s 0

  gfl-preview-lines : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gfl-preview-lines (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (buf) (off) (n) =
    if off >= n then 0
    else let take = if n - off > 16 then 16 else n - off
    in let y = gfl-rows-y0 h s + (off / 16) * gfl-row-h s
    in let t = gop-draw-text base stride font (gfl-px w s + 10 * s) y (gfl-hex-line buf off take) gfl-col-text s 0
    in gfl-preview-lines base w h stride s font buf (off + 16) n

Section: Navigation State

 The descent is two parallel stacks -- the cluster of every directory
 on the path (a negative sentinel names the FAT16 fixed root) and its
 name for the title bar. Pop rebuilds all but the last; the lists are
 a screen deep at most.

  gfl-pop-int : List Integer -> List Integer
  gfl-pop-int (xs) = gfl-pop-int-loop xs 0 []

  gfl-pop-int-loop : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  gfl-pop-int-loop (xs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs - 1 then acc
    else gfl-pop-int-loop xs (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  gfl-pop-text : List Text -> List Text
  gfl-pop-text (xs) = gfl-pop-text-loop xs 0 []

  gfl-pop-text-loop : List Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  gfl-pop-text-loop (xs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs - 1 then acc
    else gfl-pop-text-loop xs (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  gfl-cur-dir : List Integer -> Integer
  gfl-cur-dir (clusters) = list-at clusters (list-length clusters - 1)

  gfl-list-cur : Fat16Volume, List Integer -> [Device.Port] List Fat16DirEntry
  gfl-list-cur (vol) (clusters) = act
    let cur = gfl-cur-dir clusters
    in if cur < 0 then gfat-list-root vol
    else gfat-list-dir vol cur
  end

Section: Preview

 One sector answers the whole view. An empty file has no cluster to
 read and says so honestly.

  gfl-preview : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Fat16Volume, Fat16DirEntry -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-preview (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) (vol) (e) = act
    if e.de-size == 0 | e.de-cluster < 2 then act
      hd <- cursor-hide cs base stride
      f <- gfl-draw-frame base w h stride s font ("File  " & e.de-name)
      t <- gop-draw-text base stride font (gfl-px w s + 10 * s) (gfl-py h s + 26 * s) "empty file" gfl-col-dim s 0
      t2 <- gop-draw-text base stride font (gfl-px w s + 10 * s) (gfl-py h s + gfl-ph h s - 18 * s) "Esc back" gfl-col-green s 0
      cu <- if mouse.um-ok then cursor-update cs base stride w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
      gfl-wait-back base w h stride s kbd mouse cs
    end
    else act
      b <- disk-read-sector (fat16-cluster-sector vol (e.de-cluster))
      let hd = cursor-hide cs base stride
      in let got = if b.dr-ok then (if e.de-size < 512 then e.de-size else 512) else 0
      in let d = gfl-draw-preview base w h stride s font e (b.dr-buf) got
      in let cu = if mouse.um-ok then cursor-update cs base stride w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
      in gfl-wait-back base w h stride s kbd mouse cs
    end
  end

  gfl-wait-back : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-wait-back (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) = act
    sc <- kbd-take kbd
    let mv = mouse-pump mouse w h
    in let cu = if mv == 1 then cursor-update cs base stride w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
    in let back = mv == 1 & mouse-clicked mouse & gfl-close-hit w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse)
    in if sc == 1 then 0
    else if sc == 28 then 0
    else if back then 0
    else gfl-wait-back base w h stride s kbd mouse cs
  end

Section: Loop

  gfl-activate : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Fat16Volume, List Fat16DirEntry, Integer, List Integer, List Text -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-activate (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) (vol) (entries) (sel) (clusters) (names) = act
    let e = list-at entries sel
    in if gfl-is-dir e then act
      let c2 = list-push clusters (e.de-cluster)
      in let n2 = list-push names (e.de-name)
      in act
        ents <- gfl-list-cur vol c2
        d <- gfl-redraw base w h stride s font mouse cs ents 0 0 n2
        gfl-loop base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol ents 0 0 c2 n2
      end
    end
    else act
      p <- gfl-preview base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol e
      d <- gfl-redraw base w h stride s font mouse cs entries sel (gfl-clamp-top sel 0 (gfl-rows-vis h s)) names
      gfl-loop base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries sel (gfl-clamp-top sel 0 (gfl-rows-vis h s)) clusters names
    end
  end

  gfl-back : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Fat16Volume, List Integer, List Text -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-back (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) (vol) (clusters) (names) = act
    if list-length clusters <= 1 then 0
    else act
      let c2 = gfl-pop-int clusters
      in let n2 = gfl-pop-text names
      in act
        ents <- gfl-list-cur vol c2
        d <- gfl-redraw base w h stride s font mouse cs ents 0 0 n2
        gfl-loop base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol ents 0 0 c2 n2
      end
    end
  end

 The cursor hides BEFORE a repaint and is re-placed after: the pane
 covers only part of the panel, so clearing the flag without
 restoring would leave the old cursor pixels standing on the
 sidebar and bake them into the next saved patch.

  gfl-redraw : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbMouse, Integer, List Fat16DirEntry, Integer, Integer, List Text -> Integer
  gfl-redraw (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (mouse) (cs) (entries) (sel) (top) (names) =
    let hd = cursor-hide cs base stride
    in let d = gfl-draw-list base w h stride s font entries sel top names
    in if mouse.um-ok then cursor-update cs base stride w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0

  gfl-move : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Fat16Volume, List Fat16DirEntry, Integer, Integer, List Integer, List Text -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-move (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) (vol) (entries) (sel) (top) (clusters) (names) = act
    let t2 = gfl-clamp-top sel top (gfl-rows-vis h s)
    in let d = gfl-redraw base w h stride s font mouse cs entries sel t2 names
    in gfl-loop base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries sel t2 clusters names
  end

  gfl-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer, Fat16Volume, List Fat16DirEntry, Integer, Integer, List Integer, List Text -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-loop (base) (w) (h) (stride) (s) (font) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) (vol) (entries) (sel) (top) (clusters) (names) = act
    sc <- kbd-take kbd
    let n = list-length entries
    in let mv = mouse-pump mouse w h
    in let cu = if mv == 1 then cursor-update cs base stride w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
    in let hover = if mv == 1 then gfl-row-at w h s top n (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else -1
    in let clicked = mv == 1 & mouse-clicked mouse
    in if sc == 1 then gfl-back base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol clusters names
    else if clicked & gfl-close-hit w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) then gfl-back base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol clusters names
    else if clicked & hover >= 0 then gfl-activate base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries hover clusters names
    else if sc == 72 & sel > 0 then gfl-move base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries (sel - 1) top clusters names
    else if sc == 80 & sel < n - 1 then gfl-move base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries (sel + 1) top clusters names
    else if sc == 28 & n > 0 then gfl-activate base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries sel clusters names
    else if hover >= 0 & hover /= sel then gfl-move base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries hover top clusters names
    else gfl-loop base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs vol entries sel top clusters names
  end

Section: Entry

 Mounting rides the medium lock; a machine with no readable ESP gets
 an honest pane and a way back.

  gfl-run : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, UsbKbd, UsbMouse, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  gfl-run (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (kbd) (mouse) (cs) = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    let s = ui-scale w
    in if m.gm-ok == False then act
      hd <- cursor-hide cs base stride
      f <- gfl-draw-frame base w h stride s font "Files"
      t <- gop-draw-text base stride font (gfl-px w s + 10 * s) (gfl-py h s + 26 * s) "no FAT ESP on the boot medium" gfl-col-dim s 0
      t2 <- gop-draw-text base stride font (gfl-px w s + 10 * s) (gfl-py h s + gfl-ph h s - 18 * s) "Esc back" gfl-col-green s 0
      cu <- if mouse.um-ok then cursor-update cs base stride w h s (mouse-x mouse) (mouse-y mouse) else 0
      gfl-wait-back base w h stride s kbd mouse cs
    end
    else act
      let root-flag = if gfat-is32 (m.gm-vol) then (m.gm-vol).vol-root-start else -1
      in let clusters = [root-flag]
      in let names = []
      in act
        ents <- gfl-list-cur (m.gm-vol) clusters
        d <- gfl-redraw base w h stride s font mouse cs ents 0 0 names
        gfl-loop base w h stride s font kbd mouse cs (m.gm-vol) ents 0 0 clusters names
      end
    end
  end
